cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ExposureGate, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
title: "ExposureGate: exploited-vulnerability gate for dependency lockfiles in pre-commit and CI"
abstract: >-
  ExposureGate is a command-line tool that grades the dependency versions a
  code change adds to its lockfiles before commit and merge. It parses the
  staged change, a pull request or a whole repository across
  requirements.txt, poetry.lock, uv.lock and package-lock.json, matches every
  added or changed version, direct and transitive, to OSV advisories, maps
  their CVE aliases to the exposure tier in the Open Exposure Baseline
  Catalog (OEBC), where KEV-listed CVEs are CRITICAL and EPSS and CVSS set
  the lower tiers, and returns a PASS, WARN, BLOCK or DENY verdict as JSON
  and Markdown. It fails closed on missing or stale data, never uses the
  network during a scan, supports historical replay, and runs as a
  pre-commit hook, in CI and as a GitHub Action.
authors:
